<svelte:head><title>Setup guide — Discord Bot Maker</title></svelte:head>
<main id="main" class="guide glass"><div class="eyebrow">FROM YOUR FIRST BLOCK TO YOUR FIRST REPLY</div><h1>A little help<br/><em>getting started.</em></h1><h2>1. Make a command</h2><p>Open the builder and choose a template. Select a block to edit it. Connect the trigger to a reply, or add a role/channel condition with True and False paths. The list view lets you do the same work without dragging.</p><h2>2. Preview your reply</h2><p>Pick a command and set the sample user, server, channel and role IDs. Preview uses the same Python interpreter as the exported bot. It never sends messages to Discord.</p><h2>3. Create a Discord application</h2><p>Visit the <a href="https://discord.com/developers/applications">Discord Developer Portal</a>, create an application and add a bot. Keep its token private. Prefix commands require Message Content Intent; slash commands do not.</p><h2>4. Export or publish</h2><p>Export downloads bot.json and a Python launcher. Run it on your own machine or server. Hosted publishing is available only to the configured owner during the pilot. Signing in with Discord authenticates you; it does not supply your bot token.</p><h2 id="python">Run with Python</h2><p>Until this prerelease is published, install the Python package from the repository. The library works independently of this website.</p><pre><code>python -m pip install .
export DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN='your-token'
discord-bot-maker validate bot.json
discord-bot-maker preview bot.json --command hello
discord-bot-maker run bot.json --sync</code></pre><p>Use <code>--sync</code> when publishing changed slash commands. Add <code>--guild-id YOUR_SERVER_ID</code> for testing in one server. Invite the bot using the bot and applications.commands scopes, with Send Messages and Embed Links permissions.</p><h2>Save, publish, and rollback</h2><p>Your browser keeps your current local draft. Sign in to save projects across devices. Saving changes the draft; publishing creates a separate immutable version. Rollback selects an earlier published version without overwriting your draft. Stop disconnects a hosted bot; deleting credentials also stops it.</p><a class="button primary" href="/builder">Open the builder →</a></main>
